==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This level has lots of aliens and zombies. There are some Doge Darks at the beginning. It is recommended to use [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] as a meatshield. It is highly recommended to use a [[Zombie Killer]].  You will want a good Critter for the Metal Doges like Talented [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]. You might want to use a good sniper for the Spacefish Jones, which spawns as the boss. This level also has a lot of Aliens, so you might want [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] or Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] when the boss dies to quickly destroy the base. Save up cash before the boss spawns so you can spawn expensive units later.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This level has more Aliens than Zombies, so use any anti-Alien you have, like [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], etc. You can use [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] to deal with the zombie peons. Due to the unit restriction, don't send out any expensive units until the boss wave and fight the battle near your base.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
A Formicidaean Ariant spawns fairly quickly, so have [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] ready to deal with them, and save up cash after they're gone. As for the boss, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can help with both them and the additional Ariants; [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] is also useful since neither Suidae Piggicus nor Mesocosmocyclone are immune to Freeze. Your [[Cat Cannon]] should be either Breakerblast or Holy Blast depending on whether you struggle more against Axoloty or the Ariants, respectively. Be aware of every unit you spawn, because your restricted unit cap can fill fast.

